{"name":"Horn of Plenty","hex":"#bba46d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"horn of plenty","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A cornucopia.","An edible chanterelle of species (Craterellus cornucopioides."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/horn_of_plenty"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cornucopia","blocks":[{"text":"In classical antiquity, the cornucopia, also called the horn of plenty, is a symbol of abundance and nourishment, commonly a large horn-shaped container overflowing with produce, flowers, or nuts. In Greek, it was called the horn of Amalthea, after Amalthea, a nurse of Zeus, who is often part of stories of the horn's origin."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Cornucopia_Palermo.jpg/330px-Cornucopia_Palermo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cornucopia","wikidata":"Q332682"},{"title":"Craterellus cornucopioides","blocks":[{"text":"Craterellus cornucopioides is a species of fungus commonly known as the horn of plenty, black chanterelle, black trumpet, or trumpet of the dead. It forms a funnel-shaped grayish mushroom, which is found in Eurasia, North America, and Australia. It is edible."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Craterellus_cornucopioides_JPG1.jpg/330px-Craterellus_cornucopioides_JPG1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Craterellus_cornucopioides","wikidata":"Q857903"},{"title":"Horn of Plenty (Grizzly Bear album)","blocks":[{"text":"Horn of Plenty is the debut studio album by American rock band Grizzly Bear, released on November 9, 2004, by Kanine Records. Primarily a solo album by founding member Edward Droste, the album also features contributions from future drummer Christopher Bear. In 2006, the band released an EP, Sorry for the Delay, featuring tracks recorded during the same time period."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/97/Grizzly-Bear--Horn-of-Plenty-%28album%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Horn_of_Plenty_(Grizzly_Bear_album)","wikidata":"Q3140652"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Detail._Cornucopia._Marble_statue_of_deified_empress_Livia%2C_holding_a_cornucopia%2C_42-52_CE._Acquired_in_1842_CE_in_Theatre_of_Falerii%2C_Italy._Altes_Museum%2C_Berlin%2C_Germany.jpg/500px-thumbnail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Detail._Cornucopia._Marble_statue_of_deified_empress_Livia%2C_holding_a_cornucopia%2C_42-52_CE._Acquired_in_1842_CE_in_Theatre_of_Falerii%2C_Italy._Altes_Museum%2C_Berlin%2C_Germany.jpg/1280px-thumbnail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Detail._Cornucopia._Marble_statue_of_deified_empress_Livia%2C_holding_a_cornucopia%2C_42-52_CE._Acquired_in_1842_CE_in_Theatre_of_Falerii%2C_Italy._Altes_Museum%2C_Berlin%2C_Germany.jpg/500px-thumbnail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cornucopia of a Roman statue of Livia as Fortuna, 42-52 AD, marble, Altes Museum, Berlin ","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADetail._Cornucopia._Marble_statue_of_deified_empress_Livia%2C_holding_a_cornucopia%2C_42-52_CE._Acquired_in_1842_CE_in_Theatre_of_Falerii%2C_Italy._Altes_Museum%2C_Berlin%2C_Germany.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Berenice_cornucopia_gold_Collection_of_J._Demetriou.jpg/500px-Berenice_cornucopia_gold_Collection_of_J._Demetriou.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Berenice_cornucopia_gold_Co